hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15799","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, he said: I came to Umm Kulthum daughter of Ali with something of charity and she returned it, and said: A freedman of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Mihran narrated to me, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We, the family of Muhammad, charity is not lawful for us, and the freedman of a people is from them."
